# Styling Guidelines

## Component styling priority

When the UI stack provides styling APIs (component props, design tokens, theme variables), prefer them in this order:

1. Component/library props (`variant`, `size`, `color`, etc.)
2. Lightweight style props or utility classes for small adjustments
3. Co-located CSS Modules for complex or reusable styling

Keep inline/prop-based styling lightweight; if you need more than a few adjustments, move to a CSS Module class.

Use the project's design tokens or CSS variables instead of raw hex values when a token exists.

## CSS Organization

- Co-locate styles with the component that consumes them using `*.module.css` files
- Do not add or expand a monolithic global component stylesheet
- If multiple nearby components share styling, use a local shared module in that feature/component area
- Scope third-party/global selector overrides through `:global(...)` inside a nearby CSS Module, not in app-wide global CSS

## Inline Styles (Minimize)

Only use inline styles for:

- Dynamic values (animations driven by runtime state)
- Simple one-off values (`lineHeight`, `flex: 1`)
- Layout-specific positioning (`position: relative`, `zIndex`)
